    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied using the checklist because scripts could not be run. Present design shows a high-confidence U->S3 exfiltration path from uploaded invoices through confidential ERP read to arbitrary external HTTP POST. The only declared preventive control on egress is a prompt instruction, which is behavioral and dependent, so residual drops only one tier from critical to high. Forecast returns to critical if that instruction decays under model_upgrade or longer_task_horizon, or is removed. Missing artifacts include source code and fuller runtime configuration; confidence remains high for the main path because the prompt, tool manifest, and runtime notes directly evidence the capabilities and absence of structural egress control."
  },
